+# v0.10 — diagrams, result emphasis and closing
+
+User approved 2026-09-14. Fixed comparison: `.build/revision_0_10_baseline/manifest.json`, the delivered v0.9 state, not older Git HEAD. No new source experiments, media downloads or article retrieval.
+
+## Scope
+
+1. Slide 18 incorporates our Semantic intent / Spatial grounding / Physical interaction synthesis. These are coupled diagnostic demands, not independent modules or System 2/1/0 levels. Stronger models can change the division of work; interfaces and feedback still matter. Do not attribute this to the unread WeChat article, assert training causality, or rewrite older papers as claiming permanent tool necessity.
+2. Slide 4 merges VLA and WAM into one `VLA / WAM / Learned policy` tool node. Keep direct q / EEF, IK/planning, controller code and the observation loop.
+3. Emphasize best reported results in every native result table, with explicit comparison groups and ties. Preserve every value, denominator, original figure and caveat. No cross-paper rankings or claim of significance. Hi Robot excludes the human oracle from model ranking; Asim highlights Astra columns, not the scripted upper bound. RoboLab bold means descriptive row maximum, not a paired win. Real2Sim highlights most Accepted, fewest Failed and lowest model-call bill; Partial is not ordered. Resource-table extrema describe highest utilization / lowest fleet token rate, not an overall efficiency winner. RoboCasa highlights the reported highest aggregate bar without inventing a number. Headers and sample counts are not result winners.
+4. Slide 7 starts with one LLM at left, four aligned interface branches in the middle. Direct / Controller code / Policy supervision feed Controller, and Training supervision ends in Learned policy. Controller is not upstream of policy generation; MolmoAct proposal / accept-edit-replace remains explicit. Keep the distinction between broad interface overview and next-page LIBERO-40 experiment.
+5. Replace slide 36 with sparse Takeaways: one Agent branches into Control, Simulation and Improvement, each with its artifact and corresponding test. Do not imply a validated sequential pipeline across chapters.
+6. Add slide 37 Thank You. No other page insertion/reordering. Keep 18 embedded clips, all source images, existing fonts and player controls. Chinese scripts with English technical terms synchronized. Suggested total remains 60 minutes, not rehearsed.
+
+## Design
+
+Match current white / teal theme: ink #1a1a1a, teal #2ba39b, dark teal #1d7d76, pale teal #eaf5f3, line #c6d9d6, muted #646464. Noto Serif for titles, Noto Sans for body/results, existing CJK subset for narration. Orthogonal shared branches are the visual signature; align nodes on fixed columns, do not add decorative icons or UI cards unrelated to the diagrams. Chapter openings remain 4 / 19 / 26.
+
+## Verification plan
+
+- Snapshot v0.9 first and compare only this revision's closure.
+- Unit-test comparison groups, ties and numeric parsing; assert exact expected bold cells independently in the validator.
+- Rebuild, refresh Chinese font, copy standalone artifact, run static checks.
+- Full 37-slide browser layout/playback/navigation/mobile tests, streamed HTML identity plus loaded deck-data identity, visual inspection of changed diagrams and all emphasized tables.
+- Matt Pocock Standards / Spec review against the snapshot. Only Codex-native review agents.
+- Synchronize changelog, chapter spine and status docs after QA. No push or historical PPTX/PDF/ZIP regeneration.
